{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-158192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{y}^{2}<{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-|x|<y<|x|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-|x|<y<|x|}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $<$ sign, the curves are *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed lines $y=-|x|$ and $y=|x|,$ and shade the area *below* the curve $y=|x|,$ and *above* the curve $y=-|x|.$\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/c06082999e1737b6e4ea5d32a3d8d77a271e3db49c38cc3725422bcb979676d0.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cf653f6637120f3e0efe8fddef4956abeef0f68cb0b375d62f2522aa1aeb00c"} {"question" "q-158192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/6727002ca8a7ee3451f09e239f49693ec6819053525c8fbe4ce5749fd8622254.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/a11d5693c185fde49044feb92d615f5bf3496735c02e4f373e0ffa40111cc964.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/a40b0a38c8a1a6c9975e13b23db60e583d60e3b8813a4faa3f923ecfdd515cd5.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/bb8978d74f92566a81f8c4c077a37f904d22e56f66edbab63bb816e7a7c314c2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/c86e0f4cb86cfed0b6ada08c56c1582fac05b5be00a7c0ba837aa3154e2f0cee.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/6727002ca8a7ee3451f09e239f49693ec6819053525c8fbe4ce5749fd8622254.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{y}{2-x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2-x\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,x\\ne 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne 2}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed line $x=2$ and shade *right* and *left* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/2371c9724d66e0f7d74c45e173f9625a986615185c10d55c029976baa82d0877.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cf653f6637120f3e0efe8fddef4956abeef0f68cb0b375d62f2522aa1aeb00c"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/04b8028809192321180e05f2e86c5e149b4870ddb0adea7e3191e2db33f12133.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/3e55fa4f75253935fb3f372dd82612b241d1133aceaa51666fdb0513decba8ea.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/6431427a27685248942ae4ac998feeb8f38d210b63e7f4c429ce3a5bf9afd1e5.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/91094f3f8fc9b21724e4e6d0f33e2ec0dc18782b3cc0aa1d4b1e4226e4bb93bc.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/9f4dd7da9adf7ec5580f4e866fdf094e90e87425ce435feae6dc41488e6518bf.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/3e55fa4f75253935fb3f372dd82612b241d1133aceaa51666fdb0513decba8ea.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that\n\n- ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cf653f6637120f3e0efe8fddef4956abeef0f68cb0b375d62f2522aa1aeb00c"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>1}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{x-y}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4>0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x\\ge y \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0cf653f6637120f3e0efe8fddef4956abeef0f68cb0b375d62f2522aa1aeb00c"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}"] ["text" "The domain is the entire $xy-$plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/state.json" "file_sha256" "232a3d4216aab837d8ccd204c64debb0065dda813f05b06326ef276df6177f7a"} {"question" "q-158564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the domain of the function $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/